# This repo is authored on Windows and runs on Raspberry Pi OS. Anything the
# Pi executes must arrive with LF endings — a CRLF shebang fails with the
# famously unhelpful "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which reads as a
# missing interpreter rather than as a line-ending problem.
#
# The same rule AIA and Kodama-Lite both carry, for the same reason: these
# three repositories are written on one machine and deployed to another.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
*.desktop  text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf

# Served to a browser by aipi5/ui/server.py, so the same LF rule applies for
# the same reason as everything else the Pi reads.
*.html     text eol=lf
*.svg      text eol=lf

# Markdown is read on both, and a mixed-ending diff is noise in review.
*.md       text eol=lf

# Model weights are binary; never let git touch them. None are committed —
# `.gitignore` keeps `models/` out — but a HEF or an ONNX that arrives here by
# accident must not be line-ending-converted into a corrupt file.
*.hef      binary
*.onnx     binary
*.bin      binary
*.wav      binary
*.png      binary
